<td id="S5.T3.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_ll ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T3.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">(4,0): <math id="S5.T3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T3.2.5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">(4,1):<math id="S5.T3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T3.2.5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">(4,2): <math id="S5.T3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T3.2.5.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">(4,2): <math id="S5.T3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_rr ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T3.2.5.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">(4,4): <math id="S5.T3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Optimal policy</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Although an optimal policy is not strictly required for drift detection, we assume the agent follows the optimal policy for clarity of exposition.
Since we assume a deterministic policy, each action is deterministically defined for a given state.
The optimal deterministic policy can be derived from state function values (Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5 Problem Setup ‣ Detecting Model Drifts in Non-Stationary Environment Using Edit Operation Measures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) using Eq. <a href="#S5.E2" title="In 5 Problem Setup ‣ Detecting Model Drifts in Non-Stationary Environment Using Edit Operation Measures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5 Problem Setup ‣ Detecting Model Drifts in Non-Stationary Environment Using Edit Operation Measures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> shows the optimal policy derived from optimal V values.
Therefore, the optimal path based on the optimal policy is given as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S5.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Optimal path}=\{(0,0),(0,1),(0,2),(0,3),(1,3),(2,3),(2,4),(3,4)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Optimal path</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Optimal path}=\{(0,0),(0,1),(0,2),(0,3),(1,3),(2,3),(2,4),(3,4)\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p8.1" class="ltx_p">In an MDP model, when a fixed policy is used, the MDP is reduced to an MRP (Markov Reward Process) model.
Specifically, an MDP model <math id="S5.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=(S,A,P,R,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=(S,A,P,R,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> with a fixed policy <math id="S5.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to an MRP model
<math id="S5.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle S,P_{ss^{\prime}}^{\pi},R_{s}^{\pi},\lambda\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle S,P_{ss^{\prime}}^{\pi},R_{s}^{\pi},\lambda\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> with the following <math id="S5.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> where</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S5.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{ss^{\prime}}^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{ss^{\prime}}^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{a\in A}\pi(a\mid s)P_{ss^{\prime}}^{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>a</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{a\in A}\pi(a\mid s)P_{ss^{\prime}}^{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{s}^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{s}^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{a\in A}\pi(a\mid s)R_{s}^{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{a\in A}\pi(a\mid s)R_{s}^{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Using the transition probabilities in Figure <a href="#S5.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 5 Problem Setup ‣ Detecting Model Drifts in Non-Stationary Environment Using Edit Operation Measures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and the deterministic optimal policy in Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5 Problem Setup ‣ Detecting Model Drifts in Non-Stationary Environment Using Edit Operation Measures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, the original MDP model of the maze problem can be converted into an MRP model in Figure <a href="#S5.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 5 Problem Setup ‣ Detecting Model Drifts in Non-Stationary Environment Using Edit Operation Measures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.11367v1/mrp.png" id="S5.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:157/99;" width="157" height="99" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>MRP model</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p11.1" class="ltx_p">The proposed method operates as follows.
The agent starts from the initial state, selects actions according to the policy <math id="S5.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, and transitions to the next state according to the transition probabilities.
This process continues until the agent reaches the goal state and generates one episode.
One episode consists of sequences of states that the agent visited.
Despite the fixed policy, different episodes are generated due to non-determinism.
The agent repeats this process multiple times to generate multiple episodes.
The pseudocode for generating episodes (given transitional probabilities) is given in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 5 Problem Setup ‣ Detecting Model Drifts in Non-Stationary Environment Using Edit Operation Measures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> generate-episodes(<math id="alg1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{G}</annotation></semantics></math>)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>: transition probabilities, <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>: policy, <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>: start_state, <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{G}</annotation></semantics></math>: goal_state

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
          current_state <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow s_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow s_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
